hmg.manual.disabled=The HMG Field Manual is disabled.
hmg.manual.player_only=Open /hmgmanual in game as a player.
hmg.manual.start.title=Your first loadout
hmg.manual.start.body=Start with one gun and the ammunition it accepts. Hover the gun in your inventory and compare its magazine or ammunition name with what you carry.\n\nFind a recipe with the Gun Smithing Table or NEI. In Creative, take a gun from an HMG tab. Most unified guns taken from that tab come loaded.\n\nOpen the Controls menu and look for HandmadeGuns before your first reload. Use the topics on the left as you work through the loadout.
hmg.manual.smithing.title=Gun Smithing Table
hmg.manual.smithing.body=Browse the Gun Smithing Table for available guns and ammunition. Select the item you want and check every listed ingredient before making components.\n\nRecipes can require a receiver, operating assembly, barrel kit, mounts, or furniture. Build components for the selected recipe first. Some packs add ordinary crafting recipes or change the required parts.\n\nIf a gun has no listed recipe, ask how your modpack distributes it. Some packs use loot, shops, or quests.
hmg.manual.ammunition.title=Match your magazines
hmg.manual.ammunition.body=Check a gun's tooltip for the magazine or ammunition it takes. Two magazines can share a caliber or a similar name and still fit different guns.\n\nPress %s to cycle accepted magazine types while holding the gun. Put a matching spare in your inventory. Some weapons consume individual rounds or shells.\n\nPack-specific ammunition can change how a weapon behaves in Minecraft. Compare the descriptions supplied by your pack.
hmg.manual.reload.title=Reload and cycle
hmg.manual.reload.body=Press %s with compatible ammunition in your inventory. Wait for the reload to finish before firing. A full magazine, wrong ammo type, or a gun still cycling can prevent a reload.\n\nSome shotguns insert shells individually. Watch the ammunition count to see which stage has completed. Some weapons follow a separate bolt or cycling step after loading.\n\nTake a spare of the same magazine before leaving base.
hmg.manual.controls.title=Aim, fire, and pick up
hmg.manual.controls.body=Use your Fire and Aim Down Sights bindings. Check the HandmadeGuns controls and your server's key settings if fire and aim feel swapped.\n\nPress %s to cycle the selector where the weapon supports it. Stop sprinting before firing if the gun requires it. Placed weapons may have a separate setup step.\n\nTo collect a dropped gun, aim at it and press %s or right-click within pickup range. Servers can change the pickup rule.
hmg.manual.attachments.title=Fit an attachment
hmg.manual.attachments.body=Hold the gun. Use %s to enter modification mode, then %s to open the attachment interface. Put a compatible attachment into the matching slot.\n\nTry aiming after fitting an optic. Attachments are defined by the pack and can trade handling, zoom, or control. A part may fit one weapon and be refused by another.\n\nUse %s for an equipped underbarrel weapon if your gun supports it. The attached weapon can require its own ammunition.
hmg.manual.trouble.title=When a gun will not fire
hmg.manual.trouble.body=Check in order. Is the gun loaded with a magazine it accepts? Has the reload or cycling animation finished? Is the selector on a firing mode? Are you sprinting or is the weapon waiting for setup?\n\nTry %s if the gun requires the Fix Gun action. Check any overlapping keys in the Controls menu. The key to fix a gun can share a default with another action.\n\nMissing sights or models usually point to a content pack or resource issue. Confirm the same HMG build and required packs on both sides.
hmg.manual.packs.title=Content packs
hmg.manual.packs.body=Put external packs directly inside handmadeguns_Packs in the Minecraft instance. Each pack has its own folder. Install server-required definitions on both sides.\n\nBuilt-in assets are bundled with HMG. handmadeguns_builtin is an output cache. Keep custom packs in the external folder so they survive regeneration.\n\nUse the server or client log to locate rejected files or conflicting item IDs. Pack authors can adjust recipes, magazines, handling, models, and other item behavior.
